description: Standards for course roadmap and README authoring
globs: ["README.md", "COURSE_MODULES.md", "[0-9][0-9] - */README.md"]
alwaysApply: false
---

You are editing a course-level or module-level README, or the course
roadmap.

Follow these standards before writing or editing:

- @docs/standards/teaching-guidelines.md — pedagogy and explanation style
- @docs/standards/naming-conventions.md — folder, file, and notebook
  naming rules to reference correctly

Ownership reminders:

- `COURSE_MODULES.md` owns the full roadmap (module purpose, topics,
  prerequisites, production relevance, final-project contribution, status).
  It must never contain notebook sequences, exercises, or code.
- A module's own `README.md` owns that module's detailed objectives,
  notebook navigation, exercises, and minimum-privilege documentation
  (see @docs/standards/permissions-and-governance.md for that pattern). It
  must not duplicate the full course roadmap or global standards.
- Status changes in `COURSE_MODULES.md` are author-owned — draft them only
  when explicitly asked to, never as a side effect of an unrelated edit.
- Before changing a module to `Started` (including reopening a `Complete`
  module), verify its `README.md` includes objectives, prerequisites, ordered
  notebook navigation, exercises, dataset notes, and minimum privileges when
  applicable. If the design is incomplete, report the gaps and do not change
  the status.
